/-!
# Local finite presentation of a chart sliced by a regular sequence (Stacks 06MD)

Let `𝒳` be an algebraic stack over `S`, let `U` be an algebraic space with a 1-morphism
`f : U ⟶ 𝒳` which is flat and locally of finite presentation, let `Spec k ⟶ 𝒳` be a
field-valued point and let `F = U ×_𝒳 Spec k` with projection `p : F ⟶ U`. Let
`f₁, …, f_r ∈ Γ(U, 𝒪_U)` and let `z` be a geometric point of `F` at which the `f_i` map to a
regular sequence in the étale local ring `𝒪_{F, z̄}`. Stacks 06MD asserts that after replacing
`U` by an open subspace containing `p(z)` the zero locus `V(f₁, …, f_r) ⟶ 𝒳` is flat and locally
of finite presentation.

**This file proves the locally-of-finite-presentation conjunct of that conclusion, and only
it.** No part of the flatness conjunct is claimed here; see the implementation notes.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isLocallyOfFinitePresentation_algebraicSpaceStackMap_iff`: a morphism
  of algebraic spaces over `S` is locally of finite presentation exactly when the 1-morphism of
  algebraic stacks it induces is.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isLocallyOfFinitePresentation_ι_zeroLocusOnOpen`: the closed immersion
  `V(f₁, …, f_r) ∩ V ⟶ V` is locally of finite presentation as soon as `V(f₁, …, f_r) ⟶ U` is,
  the former being a base change of the latter.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isLocallyOfFinitePresentation_zeroLocusOnOpenToStack`: for *every*
  open subspace `V ⊆ U`, the 1-morphism `V(f₁, …, f_r) ∩ V ⟶ 𝒳` is locally of finite
  presentation.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.exists_openSubspace_isLocallyOfFinitePresentation_zeroLocus`:
  **the locally-of-finite-presentation conjunct of Stacks 06MD**, in the shape the source states
  it, with the open subspace supplied.

## Implementation notes

The source splits the conclusion of Stacks 06MD in two, and the two halves have nothing in
common beyond their hypotheses. The locally-of-finite-presentation conjunct needs neither a
chart of `𝒳` nor any descent: the closed immersion `V(f₁, …, f_r) ⟶ U` is locally of finite
presentation, so the composite with `U ⟶ 𝒳` is, by Stacks 03XQ at the level of algebraic stacks.
That is the same argument the half of Stacks 06LW recorded in
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isLocallyOfFinitePresentation_vanishingSubfunctor_comp` makes for a
morphism of algebraic spaces, read one level up through the induced 1-morphism of algebraic
stacks, and like that argument it is settled before any shrinking of `U` — which is why the open
subspace produced below is the whole of `U`, the stronger statement over an arbitrary open
subspace being `isLocallyOfFinitePresentation_zeroLocusOnOpenToStack`.

What is carried is the hypothesis `hslice`: local finite presentation of the closed immersion
`V(f₁, …, f_r) ⟶ U` of algebraic spaces. It is the hypothesis of the same name in
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isLocallyOfFinitePresentation_vanishingSubfunctor_comp`, namely the
chartwise statement that a closed subspace whose ideal is generated by `r` regular functions is
cut out by finitely many equations on every chart; identifying the defining ideal chart by chart
is what `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.vanishingSubfunctor_eq` reduces to the surjectivity half of
Stacks 03MB, and that identification is performed neither there nor here. The hypothesis is a
statement about the immersion into `U` alone, in which `𝒳` does not occur, and it is not implied
by the conclusion; it is satisfiable, holding for the empty family by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isLocallyOfFinitePresentation_ι_vanishingSubfunctor_of_isEmpty`. Its
restriction to an open subspace is a genuine base change: `V(f₁, …, f_r) ∩ V` is the inverse
image of Stacks 083Q, cartesian over `V(f₁, …, f_r)` by
`CategoryTheory.Subfunctor.isPullback_preimage`, and local finite presentation is stable under
base change by Stacks 03XR.

The flatness and regular-sequence hypotheses of Stacks 06MD are stated below and are not used,
so they are named with a leading underscore. **The flatness conjunct is absent.** Its source is
the flatness half of Stacks 06LW, which this library does not have: the two chart-construction
steps it consumes are named in the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/Morphisms/CohenMacaulaySlice.lean`, lines 44-60 and
following — the enlargement of `k` making `z` a section of `F ⟶ Spec k` which factors through a
scheme chart of `U ×_𝒳 V`, and the identification of the resulting fibre product with a small
étale neighbourhood of the lifted geometric point. Everything downstream of those steps is in
place, the regularity transfer across the two flat comparisons of local rings being
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/FibreRegularityTransfer.lean` and its notes. The
conditional form of the full two-conjunct statement is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.exists_openSubspace_isFlat_isLocallyOfFinitePresentation_zeroLocus`,
which carries a hypothesis equivalent to its own conclusion and correctly refuses the tag; the
conjunct proved here carries no such hypothesis.

The bridge `isLocallyOfFinitePresentation_algebraicSpaceStackMap_iff` is the local-finite-
presentation companion of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isLocallyOfFiniteType_algebraicSpaceStackMap_iff` and is proved the same
way: the universal smooth-diagram condition of Stacks 06FS is traded for the existential one and
then read on the representable source and target by Stacks 06FM, through the identity
comparisons of Stacks 04SW. What Stacks 06FM asks of the property is that it be smooth local on
source and target, which for local finite presentation is Stacks 06FC.

